      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While advanced facial mapping and rapid prototyping technologies have made significant progress, replicating micro-expressions and subtle behavioral cues with perfect fidelity is still a subject of debate. However, it is theoretically feasible that advanced algorithms and cameras could be tailored to closely capture and mimic the subtleties of human facial expressions. Still, the body double theory seems unlikely, as it would require an extraordinary level of synchrony and constraint between the body double and the mind of the original person.",
