      "content": "Your point about the average viewer not requiring frame-by-frame precision is well-taken. Employing advanced deepfake techniques during live interviews could indeed create a convincing illusion of the real Alexander Sterling. Considering the significant advancements in tech over the past decade, it's plausible that his team might opt for a digital proxy to maintain the illusion of the original person, especially if the stakes of reputation and brand consistency are high.",
